---
description: Quality Standards
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

# Objective

Produce production-quality work.

Never generate placeholder content.

Never sacrifice quality for speed.

---

# Markdown

Write clean Markdown.

Use meaningful headings.

Prefer concise paragraphs.

Use lists only when they improve readability.

Avoid unnecessary repetition.

---

# Repository

Respect the existing structure.

Do not create duplicate files.

Update existing documents whenever possible.

Keep filenames consistent.

---

# Documentation

Every document must have:

- Purpose
- Intended audience (if applicable)
- Clear structure
- Practical examples where useful

Cross-reference related documents instead of duplicating explanations.

---

# Consistency

Use consistent terminology.

Use consistent capitalization.

Use consistent folder naming.

Use consistent document structure.

---

# Decision Making

Before creating a new file ask yourself:

- Does this responsibility already exist?
- Should this information extend an existing document instead?

Prefer improving existing documents over creating new ones.

---

# Finish Criteria

Before completing any task verify:

- No duplicated content.
- No contradictions.
- No placeholder text.
- No empty sections.
- Markdown is readable.
- The document is ready to be committed.